  "$comment": "Slideshow (B10 / B17 carousel — the engine's PAGER: a stack with set.pager shows its children one at a time, CSS scroll-snap, swipe / arrows / dots, zero JS unless pagerAuto). The 7 Wix Studio Slideshow tiles, read 2026-10-19: full-width photo slides with words over them 2 (words at the left · a tall centred title) · words-only slides 1 · words fixed beside a slider of items 1 · a picture beside words per slide 3 (picture left with up/down arrows · picture half the width with arrows either side · words left, picture right, arrows top right). GAPs (what the pager cannot do yet): arrows placed at the bottom right / top right of the slider (the pager draws them in one place), up/down (vertical) paging, a ROUND picture (tile 2 — a square picture stands in), a picture layered over a soft panel (tile 4). No auto-advance except the tall photo slideshow (8 s, Pause given; WCAG 2.2.2).",
